<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Carinthia</h1><p class="st-meta">976 CE – 1918 CE · capital Klagenfurt</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The oldest duchy of the Austrian lands, heir to Slavic Carantania, which kept its unique installation rite at the Prince's Stone until 1414.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 976 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Otto II</a> separated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carinthia">Carinthia</a> from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-bavaria">Duchy of Bavaria</a> to weaken the rebellious Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-duke-of-bavaria">Henry the Quarrelsome</a>, creating the first new duchy of the Empire. It included <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/carantania">Carantania</a> and huge marches extending to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Verona</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carniola">Carniola</a>, many of which later became separate.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Dukes were installed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princes-stone">Prince's Stone</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnburg">Karnburg</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dukes-chair">Duke's Chair</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zollfeld">Zollfeld</a>, in a ceremony partly in Slovene. Ruling families included the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-eppenstein">Eppensteiners</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-sponheim">Sponheimers</a>. The population was mixed German and Slovene. Mining of lead and iron, and the rebuilding of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klagenfurt">Klagenfurt</a> as capital by the Carinthian estates, to whom Maximilian I gave the town in 1518, shaped later centuries.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1335 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> inherited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carinthia">Carinthia</a>, which stayed in their hands as a crown land until 1918. The plebiscite of 1920 kept southern Carinthia in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, though some areas went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. It is today an Austrian federal state.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-carinthia.jpg" alt="Duchy of Carinthia" width="320" height="199"><figcaption>Image: Theodore Christopher · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Carinthia_until_1946.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>976 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Klagenfurt</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Henry of Eppenstein, Bernhard of Sponheim, Meinhard of Gorizia-Tyrol</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Slovene</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>, <a href="/countries/slovenia">Slovenia</a>, <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kärnten</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1447&amp;focus=duchy-of-carinthia" aria-label="Duchy of Carinthia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5016 539 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Carinthia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5336 795L5337 793M5336 795L5362 781M5336 795L5279 723M5336 795L5229 694M5336 795L5381 747M5336 795L5380 747M5336 795L5261 831"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5337 793h0M5362 781h0M5279 723h0M5229 694h0M5381 747h0M5380 747h0M5261 831h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5336 795h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5336 795h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1447&amp;focus=duchy-of-carinthia"